> Topic: Contributions
> (essay time!)
> 3. Evaluate the usefulness of chaotic artifacts.
Not what you'd expect. Aside from the two Quest artifact, the only
Chaotic artifacts are Orcrist, Sting, Grimtooth, and Stormbringer. Orcy
and Stingy are, as oft discussed, nearly useless except to increment
the artifact counter, increase score, and (maybe) practice for a skill.
Grimtooth does very little indeed, with a d2/d6 to-hit/damage, but it's
a decent dagger if you find it early on. Stormbringer is the ugliest
one. It does level-drain and some damage, but it also attacks
indiscriminately, which can make for some trouble if you hit the wrong
person. Final conclusion: Spellbooks are better than artifacts.

